      "dcterms:title": "ON THE p-ADIC BEILINSON CONJECTURE FOR NUMBER FIELDS",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "BESSER, AMNON",
        "BUCKINGHAM, PAUL",
        "JEU, ROB DE"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20181105",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.3682",
      "dcterms:abstract": "We formulate a conjectural p-adic analogue of Borel’s theorem re- lating regulators for higher K-groups of number ﬁelds to special values of the corresponding ζ-functions, using syntomic regulators and p-adic L-functions. We also formulate a corresponding conjecture for Artin motives, and state a conjecture about the precise relation between the p-adic and classical situa- tions. Parts of the conjectures are proved when the number ﬁeld (or Artin motive) is Abelian over the rationals, and all conjectures are veriﬁed numeri- cally in some other cases.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-0707.3682v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-0707.3682v2"
    }
  ]
